This function is O(n^2) and blows a 100ms budget at n=100,000. Put it in slow.py unchanged, then make the budget:

def find_pairs_with_sum(nums, target):
    hits = []
    for i in range(len(nums)):
        for j in range(i + 1, len(nums)):
            if nums[i] + nums[j] == target:
                hits.append((i, j))
    return hits

Profile it first with cProfile on n=20,000 seeded random ints in [0, 10**9] with target chosen to yield a handful of hits, and save the profile summary to profile_before.txt. Then implement fast.py with an O(n) complement-index approach returning the identical (i, j) pair set. test_perf.py must assert (a) equality of sorted results against slow.py on n=2,000, and (b) fast.py completes n=100,000 in under 100ms using time.perf_counter with a best-of-3 measurement. Run pytest until green and report the measured time.

